  "Question": "The direction vectors of two lines are \\(d_1=(1,0,0)\\) and \\(d_2=(0,1,0)\\). What is \\(d_1\\cdot d_2\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "0",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The dot product is the sum of the products of corresponding coordinates:\n\\[\nd_1\\cdot d_2=1\\cdot0+0\\cdot1+0\\cdot0=0.\n\\]\nSince both direction vectors are nonzero, their zero dot product means the directions of the two lines are perpendicular, and the angle between them is \\(90^\\circ\\). The requested dot product is \\(0\\).",
